1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,833
Welcome to ThesisOut at thesisout.com. We start at the private research workspace, protected by Cloudflare edge bot filtering. Enter the access code and click Unlock ThesisOut to open the discovery canvas.

2
00:00:13,833 --> 00:00:32,542
Now you see the main investigation bar. You can ask a research question in any scientific or quantitative field, or click Upload in the top bar to drop a thesis PDF or CSV with zero manual typing. Watch as we type a sepsis biomarker query and click Investigate and Reveal.

3
00:00:32,542 --> 00:00:51,375
Immediately, Gemini 3.8 Flash formulates a testable hypothesis and streams live repository hits. It pulls matching doctoral theses from OpenAlex, downloads the raw tabular dataset from Zenodo, and prepares an in-fold cross-validation split with zero data leakage.

4
00:00:51,375 --> 00:01:12,125
Next, the Clue Board reveals the thirty-model cross-validated showdown. Every model is scored out of fold using probability-based ROC AUC, Balanced Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and ninety-five percent confidence intervals. Notice how ExtraTrees beats the author's linear baseline by four point four percent.

5
00:01:12,125 --> 00:01:29,208
Scrolling to the feature audit, red badges flag the exact overlooked clues the original thesis author never modeled. When we click Run Five-Stage Proof, ThesisOut runs target-permutation null testing, Super-Learner stacking, and ninety percent conformal calibration.

6
00:01:29,208 --> 00:01:49,750
Now look at the Moonshot Reveal card. ThesisOut cross-checks nine live registries including ClinicalTrials.gov, OpenTargets, ChEMBL, and openFDA to confirm commercial whitespace. With one click, we generate a provisional patent claim and download the standalone Python model and venture dossier.

7
00:01:49,750 --> 00:02:06,125
Finally, at the bottom of the page, the system schematic maps the entire compute pipeline and SQLAlchemy relational database schema. Visit thesisout.com to unlock the workspace and turn forgotten thesis data into verified discoveries.

